        "title": "Polymer Processing: Extrusion, Molding",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Polymer processing converts raw polymer resin (pellets, powder, or preforms) into shaped parts by exploiting the viscous flow behavior of melted thermoplastics or the crosslinking chemistry of thermosets. The physics is fundamentally different from metal processing: polymers are viscoelastic fluids — they have both viscous (flow) and elastic (spring-back) character simultaneously, and their viscosity drops dramatically with temperature and shear rate."
    },
